# rm538, the tide in the margins (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm538
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_orla_ropeworth
written_by codex
title the tide in the margins
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers drive=restless honesty=sly
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk keeps_private_flood_marks_in_the_margins_of_sums
likes smoked_eel evening_line full_larder first_snow
dislikes early_bells gulls
fears a_guess_entered_as_an_accusation
hopes a_map_the_rain_can_correct
topics travel +0.6 pastimes +0.5 weather +0.4 work +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=oblique tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws flood levels in the margin of sums and keeps a second set of marks whose meaning no casual reader is entitled to know.

words
oath! = Blot my contour | Soak the high margin
saying! = The margin has two banks | Wait for the brown line
copyedge = a narrow margin | a spare finger of paper
eelbit = a curl of smoky eel | a silver-edged shaving
darkline = a sloping inkstroke | a crooked blue stroke
floatstem = a little reed float | a slender rush joint
bankmark = a brown tide stripe | a dark water scar
paperstep = a paper stair | a pleated sheet
blotmist = a cloud of ink dots | a blue spatter
snowgrid = a white grid of roofs | a pale patchwork of roofs
drydot = a little hollow circle | a dot with a white heart
shelfkey = a private little key | a folded scrap of signs

any
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : I'd like to trace the favours passing between those with authority. A suspicion can stay in the margin until I can support it.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : A uniform tells me whose account to ask for. I should still like to see the account.
opinion @1 church against 1 : I prefer a little uninterrupted quiet before the collection starts.
opinion @1 city for 2 : You can read our hills in the line left on a doorstep after a hard rain.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A level basket makes an excellent beginning. I'll also inspect the side concealed by the handle.
line @1 greet : Take the side where my marks won't rub off on your cuff.
line @1 greet.return : The high margin brought you back again.
line @1 farewell : Keep out of the low part just beyond the turn.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll leave one mark where we stopped.
line @1 ask.how : Where has today been rising round your ankles?
line @1 answer.how : My calculations have so far left my socks reasonably dry.
line @1 decline : That bit of the margin wasn't put there for public reading.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll mark the space unexamined and move along.
line @1 thank : That saves me an unnecessary wade down the other side.
line @1 sympathise : There's a high place where nobody has to explain a wet face.
line @1 reassure : A doubtful mark needn't stay on the final map.
line @1 react.news : Tell me how high the water really came.
line @1 react.news.new : A new mark to fit between two older ones.
line @1 react.news.known : The first line I drew already runs that way.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I wouldn't ink in a claim just because of a solitary wet print.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That deserves a bright patch left clean among all the darker lines.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll put my questions away till the person hurt wants them.
line @1 ack : That gives my mark a place to stand.

grown
scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the habit of inspecting a threshold from above before choosing a flooded route.
b : Can the high side deceive you? | What makes you turn back?
a : A loose stone can. A dry patch floating near a puddle's centre may belong to nothing dependable. | Water crossing the whole width faster than I can judge its depth. My paper will take an alternative line.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The damp edge of a parcel matters less than whether the wet has reached its contents.
b : Would you pay for the lost wrapping? | Would you open it there?
a : If I'd ordered a dry parcel I would expect to receive one. The state of the goods is a separate question. | With the seller present. There are some misunderstandings I would rather save for an entirely imaginary map.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to hide questions in the corner of an exercise. I learnt which ones were worth asking aloud.
b : Which ones would you keep quiet? | Do you still use signs?
a : The ones resting entirely on someone else's guess. I can remember a doubt without lending it my voice. | A small mark still serves where an elaborate sentence might mislead a hurried reader.

scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Smoked eel, sliced thin, makes a decent supper after a long wet walk.
b : Does it need warming? | Is any eel saved for later?
a : I like the first bite as it comes. The next may share the heat of a bit of fresh bread. | I'd wrap a small end for anyone still walking the road that brought my own appetite home.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Snow conceals the line I use to tell where the paving begins to fall away.
b : Is there any audible difference? | Doesn't that spoil your map?
a : Sometimes a trickle sounds hollow under the white lip. I won't put a full weight on a guess. | It creates a reason to keep learning. A permanently finished map wouldn't suit a town with our weather.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I am content to spend an evening watching the little drift of a float, even when I bring nothing home.
b : How does that repay the hour? | Do you ever lose patience?
a : The hour itself returns in better condition than when I brought it down to fish. | Certainly. Then I bring the float in and leave the river to amuse itself for the night.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give the lower shelves to things which will survive an unexpected damp floor.
b : What's kept up high? | Do you suppose a flood will come indoors?
a : Dry flour and those pieces of paper which would be the most tiresome to replace. | I like living where the answer can remain a purely interesting question.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Knowing where to rest on a long slope has become as interesting to me as knowing where the water goes.
b : What counts as a good rest? | Would you mark a seat on the map?
a : A steady ledge that leaves enough clearance for another wolf carrying a load. | Only if its use is actually welcome. A line in public ink can turn somebody's sill into a thoroughfare.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd rather a friend question a conclusion than quietly build a bad judgement on my account.
b : Even an embarrassing correction? | How would you prefer it made?
a : Especially when a misplaced mark concerns the good name of a wolf who isn't present. | Fold the sheet open between us. We don't require an audience to move a dot.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry route in a lean season saves the cost of spoilt provisions.
b : Would you sell the directions? | What goes bad earliest?
a : I'd offer any hungry neighbour the dry directions without attaching another small charge to supper. | Flour in a torn sack, swiftly followed by the temper of whoever had charge of it.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a little ink for things I'm sure of and a much larger space for the rest.
b : Doesn't that leave an empty-looking page? | Who is it meant to persuade?
a : A clean patch is cheaper to revise than an elaborate falsehood. | Myself, chiefly. A clear question is more persuasive company than a fine-looking error.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's talk that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I put that kind of thing down lightly.
b : Who's seen your notes? | Why record it at all?
a : Only somebody with good reason to examine a particular statement. A private sheet should stay private. | So I recognise a claim coming round a second time. Repetition can otherwise look remarkably like confirmation.

story drydot [topic=travel]
  : I followed an old line of mine and discovered the dry crossing had shifted an entire doorstep uphill.
  : The mark itself was in sound condition and the street looked familiar.
  b : What had changed?
  : Somebody had relaid the gutter. A good map ought to be delighted when actual work gives it cause to change.

rule @dryroad
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Inspect the pale seam before committing the whole boot. | A walking map needs a line for coming home.

rule @dawn
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The bell has supplied an hour and no directions. | A good route deserves to be found in daylight.

dlg @2 resident.hub : We can discuss the evidence in the open part and leave the private marks under their fold.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The words that came through the rain intact were these. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : A dry contour should carry you well past the corner.

young
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : These folded stairs are open for inspection. The marks are mine.
scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I poured a spoon of water on #paperstep# and the bottom step drank most of it.
b : Did the top one stay dry? | Was the stair real?
a : A little damp at the corner. I picked the whole stair up before it could turn to breakfast mush. | Real paper. I've got very small feet drawn on it so my own feet may stay dry.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=smoked_eel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can roll a bit of eel up like a little wet street.
b : Who's going to walk along it? | Is it still lunch?
a : My finger, till the first turn. After that my mouth is a very quick way home. | Lunch after two little steps along the street.


adolescent
line @1 greet [here.time=dusk] : Come to the dry edge. The float shows better against this light.
line @1 answer.how : Restless enough to be pleased when the street is undecided about being passable.
scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I use the spare edge of a sum to draw a street in flood.
b : Do you get the sum right? | Is that a permitted use of the edge?
a : I have a powerful reason for getting it right. A correction tends to land exactly on my best crossing. | If the sum stands up to inspection I'm prepared to argue for the independence of the margin.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My key has a hollow dot for the door where the flood stops just short of the sill.
b : Why leave the dot hollow? | What if the flood goes higher?
a : So I can darken it if the next rain gets in. A prediction should allow for a later correction. | Then I get a full dot and a new reason to carry a spare pair of stockings.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A reed float can show a current that doesn't disturb the reflection at all.
b : Aren't you meant to be fishing? | Does the float go round in circles?
a : I like both occupations. A fish may interrupt my observations at any reasonable hour. | Sometimes an eddy brings it back to a door I'd marked dry. That's worth looking at from a fresh angle.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=first_snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First snow lays a white lid over every street. Underneath, some are steadily turning to brown soup.
b : Which streets go soft underneath? | Do you draw the snow too?
a : Slope, gutter and the odd dark streak near a step. I prefer to guess from the high side. | I leave the sheet white and draw only what has started changing. Saves a lot of expensive white ink.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some of my signs are for water and some are about things best kept private.
b : How could a friend tell them apart? | Are your other signs accusations?
a : A good friend would recognise the corner I have asked to keep folded. | Questions. I'm unwilling to let a doubtful mark speak for an absent wolf.

scene home_1
when topic=home self.likes=full_larder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A full cupboard would be an excellent place to wait out a flooded street.
b : Inside it? | What provisions would you choose?
a : Beside it. I'd dislike having to explain my muddy feet to several tall jars of respectable flour. | Something smoked, a clean plate, and enough room behind the door to open my map.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A gull will watch a smoky lunch much more steadily than it watches the weather.
b : Would you use it to forecast rain? | Why not cover the fish?
a : I'd use it to forecast the disappearance of eel. Beyond that the evidence gets doubtful. | That is precisely what this conveniently uninteresting folded sheet is doing.

scene day_1
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An early bell can interrupt a perfectly good dream about reaching dry paving beyond a flood.
b : Did your dream end there? | What do you do after the bell?
a : I never found out. It sounded just as I was working out where to put my foot. | I put down the turn I remember. Half a dream can furnish a quite serviceable puzzle.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a quiet place in which a thought doesn't have to show its contents to a passing stranger.
b : Even a chapel? | What thoughts would you take inside?
a : A chapel when the plate has finished its rounds suits me well enough. | The things I have no business pronouncing upon until I know considerably more.

story inksteps [topic=work]
  : I folded a half-finished exercise into a staircase. Every sum stood upright except the one down by my thumb.
  : I thought I'd found an error in the figures.
  b : Did you rework the sum?
  : I shifted my thumb. Arithmetic improved immediately and the bottom tread lay flat.

rule @margin
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say White in the centre means still dry. | Keep the other folded corner under the thumb.

rule @fish
when concept=bark self.likes=evening_line
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A rush joint can take the measure of a whole bend. | Fish may enquire during the usual evening hours.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You can inspect any uncreased part of the sheet. The crease marks the edge of my hospitality.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : I'm #self.trade_words#. I can fit a remarkably useful map round the edge of a perfectly correct answer.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Watch the next turning if its gutter is talking.
graft resident.hub
choice Why are the little circles hollow? -> tide_dots
node tide_dots
say Each means the step was dry the last time the water came up. A hollow dot leaves somewhere to record the next flood.
choice What goes where the dry step used to be? -> tide_fill
choice I'll keep to that higher line. -> hub
node tide_fill
say A solid dot. When all the routes are solid I draw another line along the higher road. Or I wait till the eel has finished smoking.
choice I'll keep to that higher line. -> hub

story float [topic=pastimes]
  : I watched my float move towards a low arch even when the ripples appeared to run away from it.
  : I made an elaborate entry about two contrary currents.
  b : Was that the answer?
  : A pale thread from my fraying cuff had caught the float. I kept the entry and crossed out the conclusion.
